  "notes": "USAGE:\n{詫|わ}びる is more formal and literary than {謝|あやま}る (to apologize). It implies deep, sincere remorse and is often used in written language, formal speeches, and news reports. The related noun {詫|わ}び means an apology, as in {詫|わ}びを{入|い}れる (to offer an apology). Not to be confused with {侘|わ}び (the aesthetic concept of rustic simplicity), which is a different word.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {非礼|ひれい}を{詫|わ}びる: to apologize for rudeness\n- {深|ふか}く{詫|わ}びる: to deeply apologize\n- {詫|わ}びの{言葉|ことば}: words of apology\n- {詫|わ}びを{入|い}れる: to offer an apology",
